  "issue_number": 48,
  "issue_title": "Leaderboard API only returns seeded mock data, hiding real miner submissions",
  "issue_body": "## Summary\r\n\r\n`GET /api/leaderboard` filters submissions with `Submission.source == \"seed\"`, so completed `github_pr` and `upload` submissions never appear on the public leaderboard even after successful evaluation.\r\n\r\n## Impact\r\n\r\n- Miners can submit and pass evaluation, but the public site continues to show only README seed data.\r\n- Competition rankings are incorrect/misleading for all real participants.\r\n\r\n## Proposed fix\r\n\r\nQuery completed submissions with a non-null `latest_score`, regardless of `source`, ordered by score descending.\r\n\r\n## Acceptance criteria\r\n\r\n- [ ] `github_pr` and `upload` submissions with `status=completed` and a score appear on the leaderboard.\r\n- [ ] Queued/running/failed submissions are excluded.\r\n- [ ] Unit tests cover mixed seed + real submission ordering.\r\n",
  "merged_at": "2026-07-09T18:55:10.000Z",
